<title>CANADA: Hudson's Bay completes C$300 mln sale.</title>
<headline>Hudson's Bay completes C$300 mln sale.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hudson's Bay Co, Canada's largest department store retailer, said on Monday that it completed a C$300 million sale of the undivided ownership interests in pools of selected credit card receivables.</p>
<p>The proceeds would be used to reduce outstanding debt, it said.</p>
<p>Its subsidiaries, department chain The Bay, and discounter Zellers, provide credit cards.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
